s  in the entire story and nl one of the  most interesting  [Music]  personality characters i think you agree  that enel is an egocentric maniac skypia  which is inhabited by three races of sky  people is full of conflict when we first  get there we have the tribal shandians  who were at war with the angel-like  skypeans only for enel to come in and  make enemies out of both he conquers  their land and declares himself god  ruling from the comfort of his residence  we're surrounded by pretty women with  his heavenly mantra he controls and  observes anyone who would speak bad of  him  [Music]  and in general the god theme is actually  pretty strong with eno first of all his  name nl is most likely based on the  deity enlil or l from which many names  honoring the biblical god are  descendants michael raphael ezekiel you  get the idea funnily enough enol is also  the name of italy's largest electricity  provider  now enol's thunder powers of course are  reminiscent of deities like zeus while  the metal ring with the tomoa drum set  into his back are clearly inspired by  the japanese thunder deity raijin by the  way this must be the most uncomfortable  piercing anyone ever had  [Music]  in other words oda made it a point to  mash as many different gods into this  character as possible and the cherry on  top is the fact that anal's big goal is  leaving earth and reaching the fairy  worth or as i like to call it moon  for anil the moon is the natural realm  of god so clearly he must get there  after all he believes himself to be a  god  a god complex is an unshakable belief in  one's own importance characterized by  constantly inflated feelings of personal  ability privilege and infallibility  [Music]  and so a person with a god complex may  refuse to admit the possibility of their  error or failure even in the face of  irrefutable evidence in traceable  problems or difficult or impossible  tasks  [Music]  such a person is also highly dogmatic in  their views meaning that this person  speaks of their personal opinions as  though they were unquestionable facts  and so someone with a god complex may  exhibit no regard for the conventions  and demands of society and may request  special consideration and privileges  basically making all of this a very  severe form of narcissism  i'm sure some of you just felt like i  described someone you know  please make sure they don't get their  hands on the devil fruit now  understandably all this may sound  twisted and delusional to you  because it is but anal has the power to  back it up wielding the powerful goro  goronomi which allows him to control  transform into and create electricity at  will next to blackbeard's yami yaminomi  and whitebeard's gouda guranomi it's  named as one of the most powerful and  destructive devil fruits in the one  piece worlds  so powerful in fact that it can easily  annihilate an entire island something  that the ancient weapon pluton is  infamous for so anal is basically a  one-man buster call if you want  [Music]  oda even stated that at the time nl  would have gained a bounty of at least  500 million berries if he were a pirate  down on earth simply for his power alone  but enol was not only strong and evil  terrifying a whole island he's also  charismatically smart and has a decent  sense of humor as well  [Music]  now just to get it straight anal can  come across as pretty stupid in some  ways and in some ways he is but he's  also the same guy who restarted his own  heart and built a goddamn spaceship  powered by himself to reach the moon and  here people are saying that luffy is  creative with his devil fruit enel is  not a villain he's an experience  [Music]  what fundamentally sets anil apart from  other antagonists in the story is his  arc with luffy which is also why i  strongly believe that we will get to see  him again in the story here's the deal  for most major villains in the story  just like for eno we get a decent amount  of setup just for how bad and evil they  are and indeed we do get the impression  of how tyrannical and frightening his  rule over skypia truly is plus remember  that anal and his men are messing most  of the straw heads up worse than in  almost any other arc at that point the  fact that enel himself came for many of  the straw hats unlike even crocodile was  a first that made it clear just how much  of a threat to the crew he truly was  and yet despite all of that anal's  encounter with luffy like some of the  most fundamental elements all other  major villains in one piece share first  of all we get no backstory or motivation  for his actions all we know is that he  destroyed the island of his people berka  and took an army with him to subdue  skypia what's up with that we don't know  why he ended up destroying an entire  island why he doesn't have wings where  he got his devil fruit or why he even  wants to go to the moon so desperately i  have no idea i hope you agree that anal  is the type of character that seems to  have a very fascinating and relevant  backstory and we never get to hear it  the second thing is that luffy's actions  always punish the villain in some way or  form for their deeds and and their  desire crocodile and doflamingo end up  in prison  luchi has to let robin escape  caesar loses his lap  big mom loses the vinsmoke technology  you get the idea enel however while roth  of the golden bell simply proceeds with  his plans to go to the moon as if  nothing had happened yes luffy protects  gaipia and fulfills his promise to ring  the bell but he doesn't change nl or  stop his initial goal and so to me these  two things strongly suggest that enel  might well return at some point later in  the story  but of course there is a lot more to  that now let's get into world building  oh boy  work to start first of all as you know  enel is the first enemy that openly uses  observation hack against luffy also  pretty damn potent observation hockey at  that being aware of the en